          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "MAT.15.21+MAT.15.22+MAT.15.23+MAT.15.24+MAT.15.25+MAT.15.26+MAT.15.27+MAT.15.28"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Mt 15.21-28",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " And from there he arose and went away to the region of Tyre and Sidon.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.7.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.7.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7.24",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Other ancient authorities omit",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "and Sidon",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " And he entered a house, and would not have any one know it; yet he could not be hid. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.7.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.7.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MRK 7:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But immediately a woman, whose little daughter was possessed by an unclean spirit, heard of him, and came and fell down at his feet. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.7.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.7.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MRK 7:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now the woman was a Greek, a Syrophoenician by birth. And she begged him to cast the demon out of her daughter. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.7.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.7.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MRK 7:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said to her, “Let the children first be fed, for it is not right to take the children's bread and throw it to the dogs.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.7.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.7.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MRK 7:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But she answered him, “Yes, Lord; yet even the dogs under the table eat the children's crumbs.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.7.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.7.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MRK 7:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said to her, “For this saying you may go your way; the demon has left your daughter.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.7.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.7.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MRK 7:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And she went home, and found the child lying in bed, and the demon gone.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MRK.7.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MRK.7.30"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
